{title: To God Be the Glory}
{artist: Fanny Crosby & William Doane}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
To [G]God be the glory, great [C]things he hath [G]done:
so loved he the world that he [D]gave us his Son,
who [G]yielded his life an a[C]tonement for [G]sin
and opened the life-gate that [D]all may go [G]in.

Chorus
[G]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [C]earth hear his [G]voice!
Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [A]people re[D]joice!
O come to the [G]Father through [C]Jesus the [G]Son,
and give him the glory — great [D]things he hath [G]done!

Verse 2
O perfect [G]redemption, the purchase of blood, To every believer the [C]promise of God; The vilest [G]offender who
truly believes, That moment from Jesus a pardon receives. Praise the Lord, praise [D]the Lord, Let the earth hear His
voice! Praise [G]the Lord, praise the Lord, Let the people rejoice! O [G]come to
the Father, through Jesus the Son, And give Him [D]the glory, great things He [G]has done.

Verse 3
Great things [G]He has taught us, great things He has done, And [C]great our rejoicing through Jesus the [G]Son; But
purer, and higher, and greater will be Our wonder, our transport, when Jesus we [D]see. Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, Let
the earth [G]hear His voice! Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, Let the people [G]rejoice! O
come to the Father, through Jesus the Son, And give [D]Him the glory, great things He [G]has done.
